2186279221 1113 #uuid "55f2eb2e-8042-5b14-9e44-35110ff3ed0b" 13194139534156 true] [17592186279221 1145 "First, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(1)=\\frac{\\pi }{2}\n$$\n\nThe sine function has a period of $2\\pi .$ Hence, the general solution for the given equation is\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+2n\\pi .\n$$" 13194139534156 true] [17592186279222 1000 #edb/ref 17592186279223 13194139534156 true] [17592186279222 1000 #edb/ref 17592186279224 13194139534156 true] [17592186279222 1000 #edb/ref 17592186279225 13194139534156 true] [17592186279222 1000 #edb/ref 17592186279226 13194139534156 true] [17592186279222 1000 #edb/ref 17592186279227 13194139534156 true] [17592186279222 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534156 true] [17592186279222 1041 "selection" 13194139534156 true] [17592186279222 1104 #edb/ref 17592186279225 13194139534156 true] [17592186279222 1110 #uuid "805f34c6-ecb0-553c-bf5f-d4dd8ce66e1d" 13194139534156 true] [17592186279223 1034 "x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi " 13194139534156 true] [17592186279223 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534156 true] [17592186279223 1111 #uuid "04e0318e-08ba-56e4-9438-d75356204d68" 13194139534156 true] [17592186279224 1034 "x=n\\frac{\\pi }{2}" 13194139534156 true] [17592186279224 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534156 true] [17592186279224 1111 #uuid "1eb297cf-411a-5aa9-87b9-38b0663754f8" 13194139534156 true] [17592186279225 1034 "x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+2n\\pi " 13194139534156 true] [17592186279225 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534156 true] [17592186279225 1111 #uuid "ae8f29bf-8da0-55ce-b272-7c78f6aabb32" 13194139534156 true] [17592186279226 1034 "x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\frac{\\pi }{2}" 13194139534156 true] [17592186279226 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534156 true] [17592186279226 1111 #uuid "68938b0f-1c2e-5b5e-adf2-90983c076056" 13194139534156 true] [17592186279227 1034 "x=\\frac{3\\pi }{2}+2n\\pi " 13194139534156 true] [17592186279227 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534156 true] [17592186279227 1111 #uuid "d4947629-9022-5630-acc0-b93ac1ee7057" 13194139534156 true] [17592186279228 1017 #edb/ref 17592186279229 13194139534156 true] [17592186279228 1089 "q-16228" 13194139534156 true] [17592186279228 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534156 true] [17592186279228 1100 "What is the general solution to the equation  $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}?$  Assume that $n$ is an integer." 13194139534156 true] [17592186279228 1113 #uuid "04c1e06c-4d7d-5329-b6b7-84f41d592325" 13194139534156 true] [17592186279228 1145 "First, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})=\\frac{3\\pi }{4}\n$$\n\nOur first solution lies in the $2$nd quadrant and has a reference angle of ${\\theta }_{R}=\\frac{\\pi }{4}.$ Since $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x<0,$ the second solution must lie in the third quadrant, and it also has ${\\theta }_{R}=\\frac{\\pi }{4}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979076/assets/bf1efb64724fb0dfbf60cc14905e63ba867caa0bf0edd888b35fb554af97c856.png)\n\nSince the second solution ${x}_{2}$  lies in the $3$rd quadrant, we can find it using the reference angle as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & =\\pi +{\\theta }_{R} \\\\  & =\\pi +\\frac{\\pi }{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\pi }{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution for the given equation is\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{3\\pi }{4}+2n\\pi ,\\,x=\\frac{5\\pi }{4}+2n\\pi .\n$$" 13194139534156 true] [17592186279229 1000 #edb/ref 17592186279230 13194139534156 true] [17592186279229 1000 #edb/ref 17592186279231 13194139534156 true] [17592186279229 1000 #edb/ref 17592186279232 13194139534156 true] [17592186279229 1000 #edb/ref 17592186279233 13194139534156 true] [17592186279229 1000 #edb/ref 17592186279234 13194139534156 true] [17592186279229 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534156 true] [17592186279229 1041 "selection" 13194139534156 true] [17592186279229 1104 #edb/ref 17592186279234 13194139