2186279235 1145 "At the intersection points, the $y$-values are the same for both graphs. This gives the equation $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=-1.$ \n\nFirst, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-1)=-\\frac{\\pi }{4}\n$$\n\nThe tangent function has a period of $\\pi .$  Hence, the general solution for the given equation is\n\n$$\nx=-\\frac{\\pi }{4}+n\\pi .\n$$" 13194139534156 true] [17592186279236 1000 #edb/ref 17592186279237 13194139534156 true] [17592186279236 1000 #edb/ref 17592186279238 13194139534156 true] [17592186279236 1000 #edb/ref 17592186279239 13194139534156 true] [17592186279236 1000 #edb/ref 17592186279240 13194139534156 true] [17592186279236 1000 #edb/ref 17592186279241 13194139534156 true] [17592186279236 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534156 true] [17592186279236 1041 "selection" 13194139534156 true] [17592186279236 1104 #edb/ref 17592186279241 13194139534156 true] [17592186279236 1110 #uuid "df08ff16-11f5-53e9-9812-f18963beb19b" 13194139534156 true] [17592186279237 1034 "x=\\frac{\\pi }{4}+n\\pi " 13194139534156 true] [17592186279237 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534156 true] [17592186279237 1111 #uuid "3907c9fa-acff-56a8-b049-708150e3c989" 13194139534156 true] [17592186279238 1034 "x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi " 13194139534156 true] [17592186279238 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534156 true] [17592186279238 1111 #uuid "b2aa036a-4909-50c5-99e7-b805fa560e69" 13194139534156 true] [17592186279239 1034 "x=-\\frac{\\pi }{3}+n\\pi " 13194139534156 true] [17592186279239 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534156 true] [17592186279239 1111 #uuid "e439dd9a-7901-554e-8595-16083b0c9f10" 13194139534156 true] [17592186279240 1034 "x=-\\frac{\\pi }{4}+2n\\pi " 13194139534156 true] [17592186279240 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534156 true] [17592186279240 1111 #uuid "711034d0-1346-550d-ae03-cb593210bea1" 13194139534156 true] [17592186279241 1034 "x=-\\frac{\\pi }{4}+n\\pi " 13194139534156 true] [17592186279241 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534156 true] [17592186279241 1111 #uuid "779d7901-3832-54cf-9e29-5de14bb837da" 13194139534156 true] [17592186279242 1017 #edb/ref 17592186279243 13194139534156 true] [17592186279242 1089 "q-16246" 13194139534156 true] [17592186279242 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534156 true] [17592186279242 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979076/assets/f6e3ee6eed44a5ecb7e037e9cd8401a95b3e2a4640bd4454f60019f5bd9d1e67.png)\n\nThe graph shows a portion of the curve $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ and the line $y=\\frac{1}{2}.$ Which of the following generates the $x$-values of all of their points of intersection? Assume that $n$ is an integer." 13194139534156 true] [17592186279242 1113 #uuid "0cd8eb71-b053-59d5-9b95-ce17acfec035" 13194139534156 true] [17592186279242 1145 "At the intersection points, the $y$-values are the same for both graphs. This gives the equation $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=\\frac{1}{2}.$ \n\nFirst, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{1}{2})=\\frac{\\pi }{6}.\n$$\n\nOur first solution lies in the $1$st quadrant and has a reference angle of ${\\theta }_{R}=\\frac{\\pi }{6}.$ Since $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x>0,$ the second solution must lie in the second quadrant, and it also has ${\\theta }_{R}=\\frac{\\pi }{6}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979076/assets/00d540b1f6412e4af2617452fbf0c58750d01e844d89d0d92cfacc0cb3e45e32.png)\n\nSince the second solution ${x}_{2}$  lies in the $2$nd quadrant, we can find it using the reference angle as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & =\\pi -{\\theta }_{R} \\\\  & =\\pi -\\frac{\\pi }{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\pi }{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the general solution for the given equation is\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{\\pi }{6}+2n\\pi ,\\,x=\\frac{5\\pi }{6}+2n\\pi .\n$$" 13194139534156 true] [17592186279243 1000 #edb/ref 17592186279244 13194139534156 true] [17592186